# The second lexicon, which is fetched and never shipped.
#
# WordNet is vendored a few lines above this in spirit -- data/nltk_data is
# committed, because its licence permits redistribution and having it means the
# game works out of the box. ConceptNet is the opposite case: its licence varies
# by source and is recorded per edge, and the share-alike obligation attaches to
# *distributing* the data or a derivative of it.
#
# So the repository ships only the code to fetch it. That is not caution, it is
# what lets the whole corpus be used: a project that distributed it would have to
# drop every edge whose licence it could not satisfy, and a project that does not
# distribute it keeps all of them. `commonsense fetch` builds this
# file on the machine that will use it, and it never leaves.
data/conceptnet.sqlite3
data/conceptnet.sqlite3.building
